WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.961
Let's take another look at this routing table. Do you see this 0.0.0.0? That is the default route.

00:07.961 --> 00:15.114
What that is basically saying is, all other traffic not accounted for in one of these network addresses.

00:15.114 --> 00:25.924
If traffic does not know where to go within a network, chances are it is not destined for that network. That traffic needs somewhere to go, hence the 0.0.0.0 designation.

00:25.924 --> 00:28.525
And, if we look at the destination,

00:28.525 --> 00:37.224
it happens to be the default gateway for this network, and this is the default gateway for another network, with another network adapter I have on this device.

00:37.224 --> 00:45.697
So, what this really means is any traffic not meant for either of these networks will route through their respective default gateways.

00:45.697 --> 00:52.160
And this makes perfect sense, since the default gateway will lead us out to other networks, like the Internet.

00:52.160 --> 01:05.516
For the exam, know this about default routes: that the address is 0.0.0.0, and that traffic is usually sent through the default gateway.

